---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
import { getProjects } from '../lib/content';

// TODO: Swap the placeholder avatar for a real photo.
// Drop a square image at src/assets/me.jpg, then uncomment the two lines below
// and the <Image> block further down, and delete the initials <div>.
// import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
// import me from '../assets/me.jpg';

const initials = SITE.author
  .split(' ')
  .map((w) => w[0])
  .join('');

const current = (await getProjects()).filter((p) => p.data.status === 'in-progress').slice(0, 3);

const links = [
  { href: SITE.social.github, label: 'GitHub' },
  { href: SITE.social.linkedin, label: 'LinkedIn' },
  { href: SITE.social.youtube, label: 'YouTube' },
  { href: SITE.social.email, label: 'Email' },
].filter((l) => l.href);
---

<Base title="About" description={`A bit about ${SITE.author}.`}>
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-4xl gap-10 md:grid-cols-[14rem_1fr] md:gap-14">
    <aside class="flex flex-col items-start gap-5">
      <!-- Placeholder avatar. Replace with the <Image> below once you have a photo. -->
      <div
        class="grid size-40 place-items-center rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-accent/40 via-accent/15 to-transparent text-4xl font-bold text-zinc-700 ring-1 ring-zinc-200 dark:text-zinc-200 dark:ring-zinc-800 md:size-48"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        {initials}
      </div>
      <!--
      <Image src={me} alt={SITE.author} width={384} height={384} class="size-40 rounded-2xl object-cover ring-1 ring-zinc-200 dark:ring-zinc-800 md:size-48" />
      -->

      <div>
        <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">{SITE.author}</h1>
        <!-- TODO: where you are / what you do, in a few words -->
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Robotics and embedded systems</p>
      </div>

      {
        links.length > 0 && (
          <ul class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 text-sm">
            {links.map((l) => (
              <li>
                <a
                  href={l.href}
                  rel="me noopener"
                  target={l.href.startsWith('mailto:') ? undefined : '_blank'}
                  class="text-zinc-600 hover:text-accent-strong dark:text-zinc-400 dark:hover:text-accent"
                >
                  {l.label} ↗
                </a>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        )
      }
    </aside>

    <div class="prose prose-zinc max-w-none dark:prose-invert prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-a:text-accent-strong dark:prose-a:text-accent">
      <!--
        TODO: Everything in this column is placeholder. Write it in your own voice, first person.
        Structure:
          Intro          two or three sentences, who you are and what this site is
          What I build   your interests, shown through the four kinds of things you actually make (FRC is one of them)
          Toolbox        a short list of what you work with, scannable
          Right now      fills itself from in-progress projects, plus one line on what you are learning
          Outside of robotics   optional
          Get in touch / About this site
      -->

      <p class="lead">
        Hi. I'm Aiden. I build small robots and tinker with microcontrollers, and this site is where I keep track of all of it.
      </p>

      <h2>What I build</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Walking robots.</strong> TODO: this is the thread that runs through the Open Duck Mini and the bipedal leg. What draws you to legged
        robots specifically? Balance, the mechanical side, watching something you printed actually take a step?
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Robots that learn.</strong> TODO: the LeRobot arms. Why imitation learning interests you, what you want to teach them, and how it
        connects to the walking work, if it does.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Small hardware.</strong> TODO: the ESP32 and Raspberry Pi side. ePaper displays, camera boards, the odd mechanical fix like the table
        leveling socks. The stuff you build in an evening because you wanted it to exist.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Competition robots.</strong> TODO: with <a href="https://www.thebluealliance.com/team/7461" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FRC Team 7461</a>.
        How many seasons, what you do on the team, and one concrete thing from the current robot, like the swerve drive or getting it into a
        simulator. If FRC is how you got into all of this, one sentence saying so fits here.
      </p>

      <h2>Toolbox</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Design:</strong> TODO, e.g. Onshape, 3D printing, Blender</li>
        <li><strong>Electronics:</strong> TODO, e.g. ESP32, Raspberry Pi, servo buses, IMUs</li>
        <li><strong>Code:</strong> TODO, e.g. Python, C++ on Arduino, a bit of Unity and C#</li>
        <li><strong>Learning:</strong> TODO, e.g. imitation learning with LeRobot, RL for locomotion</li>
      </ul>

      {
        current.length > 0 && (
          <>
            <h2>Right now</h2>
            <ul>
              {current.map((p) => (
                <li>
                  <a href={`/projects/${p.id}/`}>{p.data.title}</a> — {p.data.summary}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </>
        )
      }
      <p>TODO: one line on what you are trying to learn or get better at this year.</p>

      <h2>Outside of robotics</h2>
      <p>TODO, optional. Hobbies, music, sports, whatever rounds you out. Delete this section if you would rather keep the page about the work.</p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        If you want to talk about any of the projects here, or you are working on something similar, email is the best way to reach me. Links are on
        the left.
      </p>

      <h2>About this site</h2>
      <p>
        Built with <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Astro</a>, hosted on GitHub Pages. Every post and project is a Markdown
        file in <a href={SITE.social.github + '/aidenuppal.com'} target="_blank" rel="noopener">a public repo</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
